\section{Analytical Fold Geometry and Stability Thresholds}

The active turbulent sheet $\mathcal{M}_0^+$ loses Fenichel normal hyperbolicity along the 1D fold curve $\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{fold}}$. Introducing the regularized variable $q = \sqrt{e+\delta}$, the fold condition $\partial f / \partial e = 0$ is equivalently written as $\partial f / \partial q = 0$. The governing stability and hysteresis relationships are:

\begin{align}
\text{Buoyancy Destruction Law:}\quad & B(T_s) = K \tanh \!\left( \beta_T \frac{T_a - T_s}{T_a} \right) \label{eq:buoyancy} \\
\text{Control Parameter:}\quad & \Pi(T_s) = \frac{\beta^2 \ell_0}{4 B(T_s)} \label{eq:pi} \\
\text{Transcritical Activation:}\quad & \mathrm{Ri}_{\mathrm{trans}} = c_s = {{parameters.c_s}} \label{eq:trans} \\
\text{Dynamic Fold Locus:}\quad & \mathrm{Ri}_{\mathrm{fold}}(T_s) = \frac{c_s}{1 - \Pi(T_s)} \label{eq:fold}
\end{align}

Equation~(\ref{eq:pi}) and Equation~(\ref{eq:fold}) are used directly in the diagnostics workflow to preserve consistency between analysis code, generated figures, and manuscript text.

