\section{Regime Topology Summary}

The state space is partitioned into three distinct geometric regions based on local values of $\mathrm{Ri}_b$ (Table~\ref{tab:regime_summary}):

\begin{table}[h!]
\centering
\caption{Three-regime GSPT partition in Richardson-number state space.}
\label{tab:regime_summary}
\begin{tabular}{lll}
\toprule
\textbf{Region} & \textbf{Criterion} & \textbf{Physical Interpretation} \\
\midrule
\textcolor{gsptblue}{Active} & $\mathrm{Ri}_b < \mathrm{Ri}_{\mathrm{trans}}$ & Fully turbulent \\
\textcolor{gsptorange}{Hysteretic} & $\mathrm{Ri}_{\mathrm{trans}} \le \mathrm{Ri}_b \le \mathrm{Ri}_{\mathrm{fold}}$ & Bistable \\
\textcolor{gsptred}{Collapsed} & $\mathrm{Ri}_b > \mathrm{Ri}_{\mathrm{fold}}$ & Decoupled \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

